Two potential problems with setState() in multiple widgets:-

1. Data gets out of sync
If different widgets use their own setState() to manage the playlist, each widget may have its own copy of the playlist. When one widget adds or removes a song, another widget may still show the old playlist.

Example:

Playlist Screen → 5 songs
Player Widget   → 4 songs

This can cause inconsistent UI and incorrect data.

2. Code becomes difficult to maintain
As the app grows, many widgets may contain their own setState() logic for adding, removing, sorting, or playing songs. The same playlist logic can become duplicated in several places.

This makes the code harder to debug and update. If you change the playlist logic, you may need to modify multiple widgets, increasing the chance of bugs.
